package tk.darrow.tribalpower.guide;

import java.util.List;

/** Generated by tools/generate_guide.py. */
public final class GuidePages {
    private GuidePages() {}
    public static List<String> allPages() {
        return List.of(
            "SPIRIT CODEX\n\nShamanic technomancy begins with a rhythm. Raise a camp that answers you: living power, elemental workshops, woven equipment and paths between worlds.",
            "FIRST CAMP\n\nCraft a Bone Chime, Spirit Shard and Drumheart. Add a Pulse Cell. JEI shows crafting recipes; every system also works without another mod installed.",
            "SPIRIT PULSE\n\nPulse comes from rhythm, landscape and harmony. Keep a generator within 8 blocks of your workshop. Machines draw from generators first, then totem buffers.",
            "DRUMHEART\n\nStrike empty-handed. Beats about one second apart yield 24 Pulse; offbeat hits yield 10. Redstone rising edges give 5, with an 8-tick cooldown. Build a clock to automate rhythm.",
            "LEY COLLECTOR\n\nOpen sky, night, rain, nearby water and living greenery strengthen collection. Place it thoughtfully. A redstone signal pauses generation.",
            "PULSE RESONATOR\n\nSeat an Echo catalyst and place at least two different elemental totems within 8 blocks. More distinct voices and stronger catalysts increase generation. The catalyst is reusable.",
            "HARMONIC RANKS\n\nCatalysts: Echo Shard, Attuned Echo, Bound Echo, Resonant Core. Coal and wood are not fuels. Sneak with an empty hand to recover the catalyst. Redstone pauses generation.",
            "CARRY THE BEAT\n\nUse a Pulse Cell on a Drumheart or Resonator to charge it. Ordinary cells hold 200 Pulse; Greater Cells hold 1,200. Carry charged cells for spells, tools and travel.",
            "SIX VOICES\n\nEarth shatters. Fire attunes. Water binds. Spirit manifests. Air lends motion. Loom unweaves. Place the needed totem within 8 blocks of the station; missing voices pause work safely.",
            "CHALK AND CONDUCTOR\n\nMark two totems with Ritual Chalk to link them within 16 blocks. A Conductor moves Pulse through linked totems and routes Song Bench items through nearby Ancestral Caches.",
            "ECHO WORKSHOPS\n\nThe four Echo stations process real batches. Feed slot 0 from above or the sides; extract finished items below. Each has a work display and eight output slots. Full output pauses work.",
            "SHATTER\n\nEarth turns stone into Echo Shards. Raw iron, copper and gold become two grits each. Smelt or blast grits into ingots. Shared raw-material tags accept compatible ores from other mods.",
            "ATTUNE AND BIND\n\nFire turns Echo Shards into Attuned Echoes. Water binds them into Bound Echoes. Bind also turns wool into Spiritweave and dirt into clay. Check JEI for time and Pulse costs.",
            "MANIFEST\n\nSpirit turns Bound Echoes into Manifested Ingots, then ingots into Resonant Cores. Cores unlock stronger cells, equipment and long-distance automation.",
            "SONG BENCH\n\nThe original single-item workshop remains. Insert an Echo-stage ingredient and click empty-handed to sing; sneak-click to retrieve it. Dedicated Echo stations are better for sustained batches.",
            "ANCESTRAL CACHE\n\nA local 54-slot inventory for camp supplies. Hoppers and item pipes work normally. A redstone signal locks access and automation. A comparator reads how full it is.",
            "DEEP CACHE\n\nA personal 54-slot vault shared between your Deep Caches. Visiting The March attunes you; otherwise opening costs 5 Pulse. A Wayfarer Satchel opens the same personal vault.",
            "SPIRIT CISTERN\n\nStores 16 buckets of one fluid. Buckets and standard fluid pipes both work. Redstone locks filling and draining, including remote relays. A comparator reads fullness.",
            "WIRELESS CARGO\n\nPlace an item or fluid relay above its source inventory or tank. Use the Lattice Tuner on a destination face, then on the relay. Sneak-use the tuner to replace a previous mark.",
            "CARGO TIERS\n\nLocal relays reach 32 blocks. Longreach relays reach 128. Astral relays have no distance limit and can cross dimensions. Transfers cost 4, 8 or 16 Pulse per successful beat.",
            "CARGO RHYTHM\n\nEach second, a relay moves up to 16 items or 250 mB. Both ends must already be loaded. Unloaded or full destinations pause safely. Relays never keep distant chunks loaded themselves.",
            "CARGO CONTROLS\n\nRedstone pauses a relay. Comparator: 0 unlinked, 1 linked but waiting, 15 transferring. Lock the receiver with redstone when you need a remote stop. Bound links survive pickup.",
            "PULSE TO FE\n\nThe Pulse Adapter converts 1 Pulse into 100 FE, up to 20 Pulse each second. It buffers 16,000 FE and exports to standard energy receivers. Redstone stops conversion and extraction.",
            "WAYSTONE PATHS\n\nSneak-use a compass on the top of a solid floor to bind a landing. Use it to return. Keep two clear dry blocks above the floor. Power the landing floor with redstone to lock arrival.",
            "TRAVEL TIERS\n\nWaystone Compass: 128 blocks, same world, 20 Pulse. Horizon Compass: any distance in one world, 40 Pulse. Astral Compass: across dimensions, 100 Pulse. Travel has a 5-second cooldown.",
            "THE MARCH\n\nThe Gate Drum opens the way to The March. Bring charged cells and prepare a return route. March materials unlock Astral transport, the final tier for both travellers and cargo.",
            "SIXFOLD STAFF\n\nSneak-use to choose a voice; use to cast. Earth slows foes, Fire strikes and ignites, Water heals and cleanses, Air grants a short leap and slow falling, Spirit reveals nearby enemies, Loom tethers a foe toward you or, sneaking with no target, stitches you 6 blocks forward.",
            "STAFF COSTS\n\nEarth 12, Fire 18, Water 24, Air 16, Spirit 20 Pulse; Loom 6 to tether, 10 to stitch. Water rests for 8 seconds; other voices for 2. Offensive spells target hostile creatures and stop at solid obstacles.",
            "RESONANCE MAUL\n\nHold the maul in your main hand. Sneak-use a stone face to excavate a 3-by-3 plane. Each block costs 8 Pulse. Tool requirements and normal player block protection still apply.",
            "SPIRITWEAVE\n\nHood: night sight. Robe: resistance. Leggings: speed. Boots: slow falling when descending. Each active piece spends 2 Pulse every four seconds. Carry spare cells for long expeditions.",
            "RITUAL BRAZIER\n\nSeat a reusable elemental seal. With its matching totem and Pulse nearby, the brazier sustains a blessing for players within 6 blocks. It spends 8 Pulse every two seconds.",
            "CAMP BLESSINGS\n\nEarth grants haste; Fire resists flame; Water regenerates; Air slows falls; Spirit grants night sight. Redstone pauses the brazier. Sneak empty-handed to recover its seal.",
            "REDSTONE LANGUAGE\n\nHigh signal pauses workshops, conductors, resonators, collectors, relays and braziers; it locks storage and travel destinations. The Drumheart instead listens for rising edges to make beats.",
            "READ THE CAMP\n\nComparators read stored Pulse, inventory or fluid fullness, FE buffer, and relay activity. A pause keeps stored resources intact. Use clocks, levers and comparators to choreograph the camp.",
            "OTHER WORKSHOPS\n\nLattice recipes use the normal recipe manager and sync to clients. Datapacks can add tribalpower:lattice recipes using shared ingredient tags. JEI displays them when installed.",
            "THE VEIL AT NIGHT\n\nAfter dusk, the sky unfolds in slow curtains of green and violet. The March carries a colder sky. Rain veils the aurora. Client settings can reduce its detail or disable it for shader packs.",
            "GENTLE HARVESTING\n\nBrush adult Dawn Stags, Lantern Foxes and Mossbacks for renewable reagents. Each rests for one minute between harvests. Young animals do not yield materials. Breed with wheat, sweet berries and seagrass respectively.",
            "BROKEN GUARDIANS\n\nAshbound, Rootbound and Reed Stalkers haunt forests and marshes in the Overworld. All can also be found in the March. Build lighted paths: hostile creatures require darkness.",
            "BEYOND THE GATE\n\nSteppe: Ashbound, Rootbound, Rift Hounds and Echo Weavers. Highlands: Hollow Sentinels, Storm Moths, Cinder Imps and Rift Hounds. Crystal Fields: Shardbacks, Mourning Bells, Reed Stalkers and Echo Weavers.",
            "ANSWERING A SPELL\n\nStorm Moths, Cinder Imps and Mourning Bells gather visible motes before casting. Step behind solid cover to interrupt. Their magic never burns or replaces terrain. A charged staff is useful for keeping distance.",
            "RETURNING THE SONG\n\nBring creature reagents to the Echo workshops. Gentle animal harvests, Storm Wings and Echo Silk bind into Spiritweave under Water. Other hostile remnants attune into two Attuned Echoes under Spirit. Existing recipes remain available.",
            "WAYANCHOR\n\nSustain the chunk containing the anchor for 16 Pulse each second. A 2,400-Pulse reserve bridges interruptions; nearby generators refill it. The anchor holds one chunk, not a radius. Up to 32 anchors may run per dimension. Redstone or an empty reserve releases its ticket. Removing the block releases it immediately. Place another anchor at a distant relay endpoint if that endpoint must keep working while you travel.",
            "HUSH TOTEM\n\nA quiet circle suppresses hostile spawning within 24 blocks for 8 Pulse per second. It covers natural and spawner-born hostiles, including Summoning Cradles. It does not remove existing mobs, stop animals, or override commands and spawn eggs. Redstone silences the ward immediately. Keep a cradle outside the circle, or use redstone to alternate between peace and summoning.",
            "GROVE TENDER\n\nPlace the tender at crop height in the middle of a 9-by-9 bed. Supply seeds in the top inventory row and extract harvests below. It plants for 4 Pulse or harvests and replants one ripe crop for 12 Pulse, reserving one seed before storing the drops. At most one crop is worked each second. Full output preserves the crop. Vanilla and compatible CropBlock crops work; trees, cocoa, sugar cane and custom machines are outside its scope. Player protection events apply. Redstone pauses work and inventory access.",
            "BINDING EFFIGY\n\nAn empty or exhausted effigy remembers a living spirit without harming it. Sneak-use it on an eligible animal or hostile creature. Common farm animals, zombies, skeletons, spiders, creepers and the thirteen Tribal Power creatures can be imprinted; bosses cannot. A live binding cannot be overwritten. An imprint alone has no summons: awaken it through the Three-voice Binding.",
            "THREE-VOICE BINDING\n\nSeat a Spirit Seal in a Ritual Brazier. Place Earth, Air and Spirit Totems within eight blocks. Supply 200 nearby Pulse and carry three Spiritweave. Use your imprinted, exhausted effigy on the brazier with redstone off. The three voices knot 512 summoning threads into it. Renew an exhausted effigy the same way, or first imprint another eligible spirit. The recipe is deliberately a ritual, not a spawn-egg shortcut.",
            "SUMMONING CRADLE\n\nPlace a bound effigy in the first slot and Spiritweave in the second. Every ten seconds, the cradle attempts one summon on a clear, dry floor within three blocks. A successful summon costs 80 Pulse, one Spiritweave and one bound thread. Eight nearby mobs within twelve blocks pause it. Hostiles cannot be called in Peaceful or inside a Hush ward. Failed or blocked attempts spend nothing. The effigy tooltip shows remaining uses; a comparator reads them. Redstone pauses everything. Bottom automation can retrieve an exhausted effigy for renewal. Picking up the cradle drops the same effigy with its remaining count intact.",
            "SPIRIT LANTERN\n\nA carved copper-and-wood lantern brightens the camp at light level 15 without fuel. Redstone dims it; a comparator reports whether it is lit. Its animated crystal shares the living-lattice palette. Use lanterns to mark safe paths between workshops.",
            "RAIN CHIME\n\nHang the idea of rain in copper. The chime sounds softly every ten seconds during rain; a comparator reads 8 for rain and 15 for thunder, or zero for clear skies. Redstone mutes it and sets its output to zero. Use the weather signal to choreograph Ley collection and camp lights. No fuel is needed.",
            "OFFERING TABLE\n\nA low carved display table doubles as a 27-slot store. Hoppers and item pipes can insert or extract from every side. A comparator reads fullness. Redstone locks both the menu and automation, so the same decorative table can become a controlled offering buffer beside a cradle. No Pulse is needed for storage.",
            "THE SIXTH VOICE\n\nThe sixth voice is the thread itself. Loom Thread comes from Ancestor Halls and The Unsung; an Unsung Heart, two threads, four March Crystals and two March Planks make the Loom totem, a distinct voice for the Resonator. Echo Unweave reverses the lattice: ingots to echoes, cores to ingots, Spiritweave to wool, and worn Spiritgear (only tools that have taken damage) to one Manifested Ingot. A Loom Seal in a Brazier threads 2 Pulse into carried cells every 2 seconds with Luck. The Sixfold Staff gains Tether and, sneaking with no target, Stitch.",
            "BONDED SPIRITS\n\nCraft a Bonding Charm from two Spiritweave, a Spirit Shard and a Lantern Down, Mossback Scale or Dawn Velvet. Use it on an adult Lantern Fox, Mossback or Dawn Stag: three tries in five succeed with hearts, and a failed charm is kept. A bonded animal follows within ten blocks, teleports to you past twelve, never despawns, ignores your blows and sheds double reagent when brushed. Sneak-use it to make it wait or follow again.",
            "LANTERN FOX FAMILIAR\n\nA bonded Lantern Fox lights the way: it carries an invisible Spirit Light with it, grants Night Vision while you stay within eight blocks, and every four seconds marks ores within six blocks of itself with glints only you can see.",
            "MOSSBACK AND DAWN STAG FAMILIARS\n\nA bonded Mossback carries a nine-slot saddlebag: sneak-use it with an empty hand to open the bag; sneak-use holding an item to make it wait or follow. It drops the bag on death. A bonded Dawn Stag needs no saddle: use it to mount, steer with your gaze, hold jump for a short leap and sneak to dismount. It carries only the one it is bonded to.",
            "SHARED CAMPS\n\nFound a camp with /tribalpower camp create <name>, then invite with /tribalpower camp invite <player> or by using a Camp Charter (paper, Spiritweave, Spirit Shard) on them; invitations last five minutes and are accepted with /tribalpower camp join <name>. Members open one shared 54-slot camp vault from any Deep Cache or Wayfarer Satchel (sneak-use to switch back to your personal vault), count as owners of each other's camp devices, and share a budget of twelve Wayanchors instead of thirty-two per dimension. A quarter of every member's tribe standing also lands on the camp, and an Elder trades at the camp's rank when it beats your own. Leave, kick, rename and info complete the command.",
            "WORLD RITES\n\nCarve a Rite Tablet from two stone, a creature reagent and the matching seal; the seal is handed back. Sneak-use the tablet on a Ritual Brazier holding that seal. The brazier draws the rite's Pulse from the lattice within 8 blocks; if there is not enough, nothing is spent. Rain Calling (Water, 400) brings twenty minutes of rain. Sky Clearing (Air, 400) clears forty minutes. Dawn Calling (Fire, 800) hurries the night to sunrise unless the game rule tribalpower:allowDawnRite is off.",
            "LAND RITES\n\nGreen Blessing (Earth, 600) blesses the nine chunks around the brazier for twenty minutes: crops, saplings and stems there take extra random ticks and sparkle green. Still Night (Spirit, 600) hushes hostile spawning within 64 blocks for fifteen minutes, like a wide Hush Totem. Ley Binding (Loom, 1,200) ties the brazier's nearest Resonance Totem to another within 64 blocks for thirty minutes; a Conductor routes Pulse along the humming thread as if the totems stood side by side. Seal-carvers sell the Still Night tablet to Friends.",
            "LEY LENS\n\nA glass pane, a Copper Resonator and a Spirit Shard make a lens for ley sight. Hold it in either hand: the HUD reads the ley strength where you stand and the ground around you glows in a 9-by-9 grid, blue where the land is quiet and gold where it sings. Open sky counts, night counts triple, rain, water and greenery each add. Sneak-use the lens on a Ley Collector to print that collector's exact factor breakdown.",
            "PULSE LOGIC\n\nThe Pulse Gauge points its arrow at any Pulse holder and emits redstone 0 to 15 in proportion to its stored charge, refreshed every four ticks; a comparator reads the same number. The Pulse Threshold points the same way and emits a full signal only while the holder sits at or above 25, 50, 75 or 100 percent; use it empty-handed to cycle, and a comparator reads 1 to 4. Both craft from redstone, a Copper Resonator and March Stone; the gauge adds quartz, the threshold a redstone torch.",
            "CODEX DIAGNOSTICS\n\nSneak-use the Spirit Codex on any Tribal block to hear it explain itself: stored Pulse, every generator within 8 blocks with its output this second, the attunements present, the Pulse it could draw, and whether redstone pauses it. Workshops name their recipe and any missing voice or full output; relays report unloaded or locked endpoints; braziers list the rites their seal allows.",
            "STANDING\n\nNine tribes kept the Loom, one Strand each; their camps still keep time. Offer a favoured item at a Tribe Hearth for +3 standing, the tribe's reagent for +8, any food for +1, or a charged Pulse Cell for +2 per 10 Pulse. Hostile kills within 24 blocks of a hearth give +1, twenty per day per tribe; a trade gives +2. Ranks: Guest 50, Friend 150, Kin 400, Voice 800. Hurting Kin costs 25 and turns the camp's Hunters on you for a minute; breaking a hearth costs 40. /tribalpower standing prints all nine.",
            "TRIBAL KIN\n\nEvery camp keeps four Kin: an Elder who trades from the tribe's table once you are a Guest, a Drummer whose beat feeds 2 Pulse into generators within 8 blocks, a Hunter who strikes hostiles within 12 blocks, and a Weaver at the loom. Kin wander within 16 blocks of their camp and never despawn. Elders unlock two offers per rank and, at Voice, press a Tribe Mark into your hand.",
            "KINSHIP TOTEM\n\nCraft a Tribe Mark with the Resonance Totem of the tribe's voice and two Spiritweave. The Kinship Totem stores its tribe: it lends the tribe's voice to nearby stations and counts as an extra distinct voice for the Pulse Resonator, tracked per tribe rather than per element. Nine tribes beside six totems make fifteen voices.",
            "PAD-KEEPERS\n\nStrand of Soil, voice of Earth. Craft: hearths and caches. Camps stand in plains; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: dirt, moss, bread and Echo Shards.\n\n\"We never called it dirt. We called it what was left, and we kept it warm.\"",
            "GRIT-SINGERS\n\nStrand of Stone, voice of Earth. Craft: echo shatter and meshes. Camps stand in mountains; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: raw ores, grits and Attuned Echo.\n\n\"The mesh does not find the ore. The mesh gives the ore somewhere to land.\"",
            "ROOTBINDERS\n\nStrand of Sprout, voice of Water. Craft: living anchors and March flora. Camps stand in forests; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: saplings, seeds and Mossback Scale.\n\n\"Roots are the only rope the void respects.\"",
            "EDGE-WALKERS\n\nStrand of Claw, voice of Fire. Craft: Spiritgear and footholds. Camps stand in taiga; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: leather, iron and Rift Tooth.\n\n\"Boots first. Then the bridge. Then the courage; it arrives on its own.\"",
            "DRUMHEARTS\n\nStrand of Spark, voice of Fire. Craft: drums and Pulse. Camps stand in savanna; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: copper, charged Pulse Cells and Bone Chimes.\n\n\"The drum is not loud. The drum is steady. Be the drum.\"",
            "PATTERN-WEAVERS\n\nStrand of Clock, voice of Air. Craft: timed songs and automation. Camps stand in birch woods; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: redstone, clocks and Storm Wing.\n\n\"A factory is a song that has stopped needing the singer.\"",
            "COLONY-KEEPERS\n\nStrand of Swarm, voice of Air. Craft: hives and March flowers. Camps stand in flower meadows; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: honey, flowers and Lantern Down.\n\n\"You do not own a hive. You are on good terms with it.\"",
            "SEAL-CARVERS\n\nStrand of Sigil, voice of Spirit. Craft: seals and rites. Camps stand in dark forests; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: blank or element seals and Spirit Shards.\n\n\"Spirit goes where it is asked politely and stays where it is fed.\"",
            "LOOM-STITCHERS\n\nStrand of Spindle, voice of Loom. Craft: gate-paths and the reweave. Camps stand in the March crystal fields only; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: March Crystal, Loom Thread and compasses.\n\n\"The Loom was never one thread. It was nine agreeing.\"",
            "ANCESTOR HALL\n\nSunken stone halls lie in the March steppe and highlands, three rooms under Loom-wood beams with a ladder shaft to the surface. Four Lore Tablets hang on the walls and two chests hold Loom Thread, echoes, Spiritweave and seals. Hollow Sentinels keep the side rooms. Read every tablet you find: the Codex records them.",
            "DRUM CIRCLE\n\nTwelve lantern-topped pillars ring a Silent Drum in the March highlands. Strike the drum empty-handed or with a Bone Chime: four beats about a second apart (16 to 28 ticks) wake what waits beneath. A wrong beat thuds and resets. Each drum answers once per twenty minutes of real time, and never while its keeper is already awake.",
            "THE UNSUNG\n\nA hollow drum-spirit with two rune arms and a cracked mask. Beat (above two thirds health): a shockwave every 3 seconds hits everyone within 8 blocks for 6 and knocks back; sneak to brace for half damage and no knockback; its swipe deals 10. Chorus: every 8 seconds it calls two Echo Weavers, up to six, and beats faster. Silence (below one third): it goes invulnerable over the drum and casts slow weaving bolts. Strike the Silent Drum with the four-beat to resync it: stunned 8 seconds at double damage, then silence returns 12 seconds after the resync. Drops an Unsung Heart, 16 to 24 Loom Thread and 4 Resonant Cores. Leave for 30 seconds and it resets.",
            "CRYSTAL SPIRE\n\nA tapering spire of March Crystal in the crystal fields, with a Loom-stitcher waystation at its foot: a hearth, a banner, a Loom totem and one Elder of the Spindle tribe. It is the only camp the Loom-stitchers keep, and the place to trade for Loom Thread once you are their friend.",
            "TABLET: PAD-KEEPERS' HEARTH\n\nWe never called it dirt. We called it what was left, and we kept it warm. When the ground fell away we carried it in baskets, a pad at a time, and set a hearth on every pad we saved. Feed the hearth bread and moss. It remembers who fed it.",
            "TABLET: GRIT-SINGERS' MESH\n\nThe mesh does not find the ore. The mesh gives the ore somewhere to land. Sing low over raw stone and it loosens; sing lower and it shatters into echo. Our meshes still hang in the halls, humming to nothing. Bring them ore and they will hum to you.",
            "TABLET: ROOTBINDERS' ROPE\n\nRoots are the only rope the void respects. We planted the first anchors on the falling islands and bound them island to island, root to root. Half of them held. Plant a sapling in the March soil and you will feel it pull toward the others.",
            "TABLET: EDGE-WALKERS' BOOTS\n\nBoots first. Then the bridge. Then the courage; it arrives on its own. We walked the rift edge where the thread frayed thinnest and set footholds for the rest. A foothold is iron, leather and a promise not to look down.",
            "TABLET: DRUMHEARTS' BEAT\n\nThe drum is not loud. The drum is steady. Be the drum. One beat a breath apart, and the copper answers; miss a beat and it forgets you. Every engine in the March still keeps our time. Strike, wait, strike. That is the whole of it.",
            "TABLET: PATTERN-WEAVERS' SONG\n\nA factory is a song that has stopped needing the singer. We wrote the timings on clock-wheels and moth dust and let the Loom carry the tune. When the Cut came the songs kept playing. Some are playing still. Listen for the click before the hum.",
            "TABLET: COLONY-KEEPERS' HIVE\n\nYou do not own a hive. You are on good terms with it. Offer honey, plant the March flowers, and the swarm will route Pulse through the comb for you. Take without asking and the comb goes quiet. It is very patient about this.",
            "TABLET: SEAL-CARVERS' RITE\n\nSpirit goes where it is asked politely and stays where it is fed. A seal is a polite request carved in stone. A brazier is the meal. We cut blank seals by the thousand before the Cut, and asked for far too much. Ask for a little. Feed it well.",
            "TABLET: LOOM-STITCHERS' THREAD\n\nThe Loom was never one thread. It was nine agreeing. We held the Spindle and stitched the tribes' strands into one cloth over the sky. When eight pulls became eight arguments, the cloth tore along our seam. We are still stitching. Bring crystal. Bring thread.",
            "TABLET: THE CUT\n\nNo one struck the Loom. It was pulled from nine sides until one strand gave, and then the rest went like a rope through a hand. The continents fell in the space of a drum-roll. What did not fall drifted into the March and sank slow. Nine tribes, one hall, no one to blame.",
            "TABLET: THE UNSUNG\n\nA drum was carried out of every falling camp so the beat would not stop. The last drum was carried into the circle and no one was left to strike it. Its keeper went hollow waiting. Wake it with the four-beat and it will rise to be struck. Sneak when it beats. Resync it when it goes silent. It only wants the rhythm back.",
            "TABLET: THE MARCH\n\nThe March is where the thread frayed thinnest and the fallen ground came to rest. Halls lie sunk to the lintel; camps keep time with no one at the drum; crystal grows where the Loom's tension still pools. Walk it with a full Pulse cell and a steady hand. Everything here still answers a beat.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: YOUR FIRST CAMP\n\n1. Find a tribe camp: a hearth, a banner and four Kin in plains, mountains, forest, taiga, savanna, birch woods, flower meadows or dark forest. The banner colour names the tribe; the tribe pages list what each favours.\n2. Read the hearth. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on it, or simply watch what the Kin carry: bread and moss for Pad-keepers, ores for Grit-singers, saplings for Rootbinders.\n3. Offer. Use a favoured item on the Tribe Hearth for +3 standing, or the tribe's reagent for +8. Any food gives +1 and a charged Pulse Cell gives +2 per 10 Pulse. Seventeen favoured offerings, or seven reagents, reach Guest at 50.\n4. Trade. Use the Elder once you are a Guest. Every trade gives +2, and each rank unlocks two more offers.\n5. Keep the peace. Never hit Kin (-25 standing and an angry Hunter for a minute) and never break the hearth (-40). Kills of hostiles within 24 blocks of the hearth earn +1, twenty times a day.\nWhat you now have: Guest standing with one tribe, its first trades, and a hearth that remembers you. /tribalpower standing prints all nine.\nNext: Friend at 150 opens the seal and tablet trades; Voice at 800 earns a Tribe Mark, the key to a Kinship Totem.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: THE SIXTH VOICE\n\n1. Loot an Ancestor Hall. The sunken halls in the March steppe and highlands keep Loom Thread in their two chests; read the four tablets on the way out.\n2. Carve a Loom Seal: a Blank Seal, one Loom Thread and a Spirit Shard, shapeless. Seat it in a Ritual Brazier with Pulse nearby to thread 2 Pulse into your carried cells every two seconds.\n3. Build Echo Unweave: March Stone around a Copper Resonator, a Spirit Shard and two Loom Thread. It needs the Loom voice within 8 blocks, which for now only a Kinship Totem of the Loom-stitchers or a Loom-stitcher camp can lend.\n4. Wake The Unsung at a Drum Circle (see that walkthrough) and take its Unsung Heart.\n5. Craft the Loom totem: four March Crystal, two Loom Thread, two March Planks around the Unsung Heart. Place it within 8 blocks of the Unweave and of a Pulse Resonator.\nWhat you now have: the sixth voice. Unweave turns ingots back to echoes, cores to ingots, Spiritweave to wool and damaged Spiritgear into one Manifested Ingot; the Resonator counts one more distinct voice.\nNext: the Sixfold Staff's Loom voice (Tether and Stitch) and the Ley Binding rite, which needs the Loom seal.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: WAKE THE UNSUNG\n\n1. Prepare: full Pulse cells, food, a Bone Chime, and a bound return route. Bring a friend if you can; the fight lasts a few minutes.\n2. Find a Drum Circle in the March highlands: twelve lantern pillars around a Silent Drum.\n3. Beat four times. Strike the drum empty-handed or with the chime, about one second apart (16 to 28 ticks). A wrong beat thuds and resets the count. The drum answers once per twenty minutes and never while its keeper is awake.\n4. Beat phase: every three seconds a shockwave hits everyone within 8 blocks for 6 and knocks back. Sneak just before it lands to brace: half damage, no knockback. Its swipe deals 10, so keep the drum between you.\n5. Chorus, below two thirds health: it calls two Echo Weavers every eight seconds, up to six, and beats faster. Clear the weavers before they slow you.\n6. Silence, below one third: it hovers invulnerable over the drum and casts slow weaving bolts. Walk to the drum and play the four-beat again to resync it: eight seconds stunned at double damage. Silence returns twelve seconds after each resync, so repeat.\nWhat you now have: an Unsung Heart, 16 to 24 Loom Thread and 4 Resonant Cores. Leaving for thirty seconds resets the fight.\nNext: the Loom totem (The sixth voice) and the Loom-stitcher trades at the Crystal Spire.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: YOUR FIRST RITE\n\n1. Choose the rite. Rain Calling needs the Water seal and 400 Pulse; Sky Clearing the Air seal and 400. Dawn Calling (Fire, 800) and the land rites cost more. Start with rain.\n2. Carve the tablet: two stone, the rite's creature reagent (a Reed Fang for rain) and the matching seal, shapeless. The seal is handed back.\n3. Seat the seal. Use the Water Seal on a Ritual Brazier; the brazier's usual blessing still runs, and the seal stays reusable.\n4. Gather 400 Pulse within 8 blocks of the brazier: a charged Greater Pulse Cell in a Drumheart, a Resonator with a good catalyst, or several generators together. A Pulse Gauge or the Codex diagnostics show the total.\n5. Cast. Sneak-use the tablet on the brazier. If the lattice holds less than the cost nothing is spent; otherwise the tablet is consumed and the Pulse drawn.\nWhat you now have: twenty minutes of rain (or forty minutes of clear sky), stronger Ley Collectors, and a brazier that knows how to answer tablets.\nNext: Green Blessing over your farm (Earth, 600), Still Night around the camp (Spirit, 600), or Ley Binding between two distant totems (Loom, 1,200).",
            "WALKTHROUGH: BOND A FAMILIAR\n\n1. Craft a Bonding Charm: two Spiritweave, a Spirit Shard and one reagent of the animal you want (Lantern Down, Mossback Scale or Dawn Velvet). Brush an adult of that species to get the reagent.\n2. Find an adult Lantern Fox (forests, dusk), Mossback (swamps) or Dawn Stag (forests, dawn). Young animals cannot be bonded.\n3. Use the charm on it. Three tries in five succeed with hearts; a failed charm is kept, so try again.\n4. Follow and stay. The familiar follows within ten blocks and teleports to you past twelve. Sneak-use it (empty-handed for a Mossback) to make it wait, and again to follow. It never despawns and ignores your blows.\n5. Learn its trick. Fox: an invisible Spirit Light travels with it, Night Vision within eight blocks, and ore glints only you can see. Mossback: sneak-use with an empty hand for a nine-slot saddlebag. Stag: use it to ride without a saddle, steer with your gaze, hold jump to leap, sneak to dismount.\n6. Brush it. A bonded animal sheds double reagent, once a minute.\nWhat you now have: a companion that lights, carries or carries you, and a renewable reagent supply.\nNext: Rootbinders favour Mossback Scale and Colony-keepers Lantern Down, so a brushed familiar also buys standing.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: FOUND A CAMP\n\n1. Found it: /tribalpower camp create <name>. You become its first member.\n2. Invite. Craft a Camp Charter (paper, Spiritweave, Spirit Shard) and use it on a player, or run /tribalpower camp invite <player>. Invitations last five minutes; the invitee accepts with /tribalpower camp join <name>.\n3. Share the vault. Open any Deep Cache or Wayfarer Satchel: sneak-use switches between your personal vault and the shared 54-slot camp vault.\n4. Share the devices. Members count as owners of each other's camp devices: cradles, tenders, anchors and locked menus open for all of you.\n5. Budget anchors. The camp shares twelve Wayanchors per dimension instead of thirty-two each, so agree on which chunks matter.\n6. Manage it: /tribalpower camp info, rename, kick and leave. A quarter of every member's tribe standing lands on the camp, and an Elder trades at the camp's rank when it beats your own.\nWhat you now have: a named camp with one vault, shared devices and pooled tribe standing.\nNext: the Shared camps teaching for the fine print, and Kinship Totems to lend your camp every tribe's voice.",
            "DAWN STAG\n\nA dawn grazer that carries the old forest song in its antlers. Breed with wheat; brush adults for Dawn Velvet. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm to ride it without a saddle.",
            "LANTERN FOX\n\nA shy dusk forager whose tail marks safe paths. Breed with sweet berries; brush adults for Lantern Down. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm for a lantern that follows you.",
            "MOSSBACK\n\nA patient wetland gardener with a living shell. Breed with seagrass; brush adults for a naturally shed Mossback Scale. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm for a walking saddlebag.",
            "ASHBOUND\n\nThe remains of a broken fire rite. Its melee strikes briefly ignite; keep water close.",
            "ROOTBOUND\n\nA grove guardian twisted by a severed ley line. Slow but sturdy; its blows root travellers briefly.",
            "REED STALKER\n\nA marsh hunter concealed among spirit reeds. Fast strikes carry a short poison.",
            "SHARDBACK\n\nA crystal-field scavenger armored in singing stone. Keep your distance from its heavy shove.",
            "HOLLOW SENTINEL\n\nAn empty watchman that still guards the ancient roads. Its touch weakens the grip of attackers.",
            "STORM MOTH\n\nA storm-fed spirit with vast veil wings. A bright gathering of motes warns of its gust; cover breaks the attack.",
            "CINDER IMP\n\nA nimble ember spirit. It gathers sparks before a burning bolt; the spell never ignites terrain.",
            "MOURNING BELL\n\nA floating relic that remembers the lost tribes. Its telegraphed chime slows; shelter interrupts the song.",
            "RIFT HOUND\n\nA hunter drawn to tears in the lattice. It closes distance quickly but cannot cross worlds by itself.",
            "ECHO WEAVER\n\nAn eight-legged keeper of broken songs. Its bite slows prey without placing webs or damaging the camp."
        );
    }
}
